# Written before the first commit, deliberately.
#
# The job-hunt repo's .gitignore opens by saying that the session file and
# every key stayed out of git only because this file existed first. The same
# reasoning applies harder here: this project will hold an Apify token, a
# Serper key, a Supabase connection string and an n8n API key, and any one of
# them in a public commit is a rotation emergency.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials*.json
service-account*.json
*.pem
*.key

# --- Data. Nothing scraped or downloaded belongs in git. ---
# Overture / Foursquare parquet is hundreds of MB and is re-downloadable.
# Lead data is personal data about real businesses; it stays in Postgres.
data/
*.parquet
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.db
*.sqlite

# --- Fixtures are the exception: saved HTML is the whole point of the
#     offline test loop, so tests/fixtures/ is tracked on purpose. ---

# --- Tooling noise ---
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
